{"name":"Crimson Garland","hex":"#982531","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crimson","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, slightly bluish red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a deep red colour.","Immodest. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crimson"},{"term":"garland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A circular or linear decoration, especially one of plaited flowers or leaves, worn on the body or draped as a decoration.","An accolade or mark of honour."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To deck or ornament something with a garland.","To form something into a garland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garland"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crimson","blocks":[{"text":"Crimson is a rich, deep red color, inclining to purple. It originally meant the color of the kermes dye produced from a scale insect, Kermes vermilio, but the name is now sometimes also used as a generic term for slightly bluish-red colors that are between red and rose. It is the national color of Nepal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg/330px-Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson","wikidata":"Q303826"},{"title":"Garland","blocks":[{"text":"A garland is a decorative braid, knot or wreath of flowers, leaves, or other material. Garlands can be worn on the head or around the neck, hung on an inanimate object, or laid in a place of cultural or religious importance. In contemporary times, garlands are used to decorate, especially around holidays."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Choinka.JPG/330px-Choinka.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garland","wikidata":"Q756600"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https: